# Legacy Scout

## Lore

The Legacy Scout is a woodsman, archaeologist, historian and treasure hunter in one. Where other Wilderness Scouts follow plants or animals, this one follows the past: the ruins of the Time Before the Rifts, buried by centuries and swallowed by the wilderness. Legacy Scouts find, excavate and identify authentic pre-Rifts artifacts, and they value what a site can teach about Earth''s history over what its relics would sell for.

They are often found with Rogue Scholars, historians and scientists, and have the most book learning of any Wilderness Scout, yet they are just as much at home with woodcraft and wildlife. Their alignments lean toward Unprincipled, Anarchist and Aberrant, because for too many of them the relics of the past come to matter more than people.

## GM Notes

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: four medium and two large specimen containers, a box of 100 gallon-size zippered plastic bags, 1D4+2 large pieces of white chalk, a can of fluorescent orange or yellow spray paint, 1D4 waterproof sacks, a 20-foot (6.1 m) spool of wire, two demolition charges, nine rock climbing spikes or pitons, a hammer and chisel, four heavy iron spikes, an ice pick, a brush and other digging and excavation tools, a block and tackle, a folding utility knife, a dozen pencil-sized chemical lights and multi-optics goggles. A character with a Computer skill has a portable or pocket computer.

Weapons: one for each W.P. with 1D4 E-Clips each, a Vibro-Knife, and one weapon that is probably an authentic pre-Rifts piece, often still carrying NEMA or US Military markings and regarded as lucky.

Money: besides 2D6x100 credits, 4D4x1000 credits worth of pre-Rifts relics and one significant artifact worth 2D6x1000 credits (a book, artwork, weapon, disk or the like) that historians, collectors and Coalition officers would recognize. The Coalition States outlaw most such artifacts.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'legacy-scout');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'legacy-scout';

